Package: infocentroid
Title: Information-Dense Centroid Metrics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Ahmet", "Kutuk", email = "ahmetkutuk@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Traditional central tendency and dispersion measures such as the
    mean and standard deviation can be misleading for multimodal or
    outlier-contaminated data. This package implements information-theoretic
    alternatives that weight observations by their local probability density,
    focusing on the region containing the bulk of the data. The core functions
    include ic_weights() for kernel density or histogram based entropy
    weighting, ic_center() and ic_dispersion() for weighted location and
    spread, ic_combined() for a single information density score between zero
    and one, and ic_plot() for visualization.
